            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Tamil for a pillar, then the Tamil for a gutter."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: திருகு",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "திருகு — tiruku — \"to screw; to twist\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "அவன் ஒரு புதிய குமிழைக் கதவில் திருகினான். avaṉ oru putiya kumiḻaik katavil tirukiṉāṉ. He screwed a new knob onto the door."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (I …): திருகினேன், tirukiṉēṉ."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The same word is a noun: ஒரு திருகு (tiruku), a screw."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "திருகு (tiruku) is native Dravidian: DEDR 3246, under திரி (tiri), \"to turn\", gives திருகு (tiruku), \"to twist, to wring\", and the noun \"a twist, a screw thread\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for describing what you lived and felt."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
